WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Today we are ringing the school bell and unlocking the every day Russian words that let you talk about classes, teachers and learning adventures. I'm Olya, and this is привет, Русский, episode 68. Our word of the day is Uчитель. Uчитель. Say it with me slowly. Uчитель. It means teacher. Imagine your teacher cheering you can do it. The cheer sound in Uчитель helps you remember the friendly guided school. Repeat after me.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:56.300
Uчитель. Now listen to it in a sentence. Мой учитель говорит по-русски, my teacher speaks Russian. Let's build more words for school life. The first one is school. It means school. I'm going to school. School starts with the same sound as school in English. This makes the word easy to remember right away. Repeat after me.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:11.140
Next comes Uрок. Uрок. It means lesson. Uрок начинается в 9. The lesson starts at 9. Uрок sounds like Uрок. Your lesson rocks when you learn new things. Repeat after me. Uрок.

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:18.160
Now we have книга. Книга. It means book. Учитель читает книгу. The teacher reads the book.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:26.720
Picture a knee holding a gun on your lap while reading. This image helps fix the word in mind. Repeat after me. Книга.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:33.800
Here is писать. Писать. It means to write. Дети пишут в тетраде. Children write in a notebook.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:40.960
Писать sounds like писать. The piece sits and writes in the notebook. Repeat after me. Писать.

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:47.000
Next is читать. Читать. It means to read. Я читаю книгу. I read a book.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:54.180
Читать is like чита racing through pages fast. The чита moves quickly across the words. Repeat after me.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:02:01.440
Читать. Say ручка. Ручка. It means pen. Дай мне ручку, пожалуйста. Give me a pen, please.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:09.360
Руч fits in your hand like a little cuff friend. The pen stays closed during writing time. Repeat after me. Ручка.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:17.360
Now try class. Класс. It means class or classroom. Класс большой и светлый. The class is big and bright.

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:25.620
Класс sounds exactly like class in English. The sound stays the same across both languages. Repeat after me. Класс.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:33.380
One more word is друк. Друк. It means friend. Мой друк сидит рядом. My friend sits next to me.

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:41.620
Your drug is the body who drums up fun at school. The friend brings energy to every lesson. Repeat after me. Друк.

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:50.360
Let's look at one simple grammar idea using the word читать. Russian verbs change their endings depending on who is doing the action.

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:58.960
Я читаю means I read. Ты читаешь means you read. Он читает, or она читает, means he reads or she reads.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:06.140
The ending tells you right away who is reading. That is different from English, where the verb often stays the same.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:14.840
There's something really cool about one of today's words that takes us back in time. The Russian word школа once meant three times.

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:26.520
It started in ancient Greek as Schole, describing leisure for thinking and talking. Greek ideas moved into Latin as Schole, then reached old Russian in the 17th century.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:36.340
English kept a softer sound while Russian kept the originals her sound. Picture Greek thinkers turning the acquired three time into lively classrooms.

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:45.740
That same peaceful idea became the slower Schole we used today. In Russia the first day of school on September 1 is called Денин Знани.

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:53.060
Children bring flowers to their teachers. The whole school gathers for a special assembly to welcome the new year of learning.

00:03:53.060 --> 00:04:01.940
For kids, draw a picture of your classroom and label three things with today's words. For adults, imagine meeting a new Russian classmate.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:10.120
Introduce yourself and mention one thing you like about school using at least two new words. Молодец, that means well done.

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:19.680
Remember, every expert started as a beginner. Practice saying today's words out loud even just once, and you'll be amazed how fast you learn.

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:30.360
See you next time. Пока. That's Russian for buy. And if you'd rather watch then listen, find us on YouTube at NerRU, links in the show notes.

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:37.080
